			"Message": "chore(Element): Advance to Wind IPC primitives and tracing utilities\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to commit 4d997a51, incorporating the latest changes from the Wind service layer.\n\nThis update introduces `MountainInvoke.ts` to encapsulate raw Tauri invocation logic (`InvokeMountain`, `InvokeViaNode`), centralizing native backend communication for the Wind architecture. Additionally, `Trace.ts` is added to provide non-invasive diagnostic tools (`Trace`, `DevLogForward`, `TimedTrace`) for OTEL performance collection and log mirroring to `Mountain.dev.log`.\n\nThese changes eliminate code duplication in the routing layer and establish a standardized observability surface, enabling structured error handling and performance monitoring across the editor's service layer.",
			"SHA": "b1213928406a3bce52a7c77e65b35176f136555d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:28:07Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Update submodule with Wind IPC routing and stub channels\n\nAdvance the Element submodule to commit 989e00d0, which incorporates updates from the Wind service layer.\n\nThe update introduces `ChannelRouteMap` to translate VS Code IPC channel names into Mountain `method:` prefixes, ensuring `TauriChannel.call` correctly dispatches requests to the native backend. It also establishes `StubChannels` to provide safe, typed default responses for unimplemented shared-process channels (e.g., sync, telemetry, webviews).\n\nThese changes prevent `Unknown method` runtime errors and undefined crashes by intercepting unimplemented IPC calls and returning plausible empty states, ensuring UI stability while native handlers are progressively implemented across the editor architecture.",
			"SHA": "ea1a2c1df38a5077df082cfbaa9473f5e3b8b93a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:26:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Advance Element submodule with Air modularization and Output type fix\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to commit 30aab8c0, incorporating two critical upstream changes from its own dependencies.\n\nAdvance the Air submodule to v1.3.0, which introduces strict modularization of the daemon sidecar by extracting CLI, Downloader, Plugins, and Updates subsystems into dedicated modules. This refactor enforces separation of concerns and adds domain-specific value types, hierarchical `CommandTypes` dispatch, token-bucket `RateLimit` logic, and `EventBus` publish/subscribe mechanisms.\n\nSimultaneously, update the Output submodule to v25.9.1 to resolve a `@types/node` dependency patch. This ensures TypeScript safety for the bundled VS Code platform code consumed by the Cocoon extension host.\n\nThese updates align the native daemon architecture with project effect-based principles and maintain strict dependency hygiene.",
			"SHA": "f24f54fe1393f7ee7651f47bee1a981aae5161e6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:18:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				19
			],
			"Message": "chore(Maintain): Normalize shell syntax and redirect spacing across build scripts\n\nApply consistent indentation and operator placement to the Maintain directory shell utilities to align with project linting standards. Standardize redirect operators (e.g., `2> /dev/null` with space, `>/dev/null` without space where appropriate) and remove inconsistent leading tabs in `case` block bodies.\n\nKey changes:\n- **Debug/Build.sh, Run.sh, Dev-Mountain.sh, Release.sh, Release/Build.sh**: Standardize `case` statement indentation for options and profile blocks; ensure consistent spacing in `grep`, `du`, and `find` command redirections.\n- **Format.sh, Profile.sh, Save.sh**: Fix `dirname` pipeline redirections and `case` block styling.\n- **Integration/SmokeProfiles.sh**: Align `kill`, `wait`, and `grep` redirection spacing; standardize `||` operator placement for error handling.\n- **Script/* (CleanGenerated, GenerateRouteManifest, PostHogCapture, etc.)**: Unify `2> /dev/null` usage, fix `cat` and `echo` redirection spacing, and ensure `find`/`xargs` pipelines maintain consistent formatting.\n- **Test/TelemetryTreeShake.sh**: Standardize `strings` and `grep` redirections and `wc` command piping.\n\nThese changes ensure all shell scripts pass `shfmt` and `shellcheck` without warnings, improving CI reliability and code consistency.\n\nRefs #e363785695a702badc0d40679e2c77280a233e2a",
			"SHA": "0f4b5f41de621741bc76169f30dce8b811b4c248"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T01:18:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				18
			],
			"Message": "chore(Maintain): Normalize shell syntax and formatting across build scripts\n\nApply consistent indentation and operator placement to the Maintain directory scripts to align with project linting standards. Remove unnecessary leading tabs in `case` blocks and standardize redirect operators (e.g., `2>/dev/null` instead of `2> /dev/null`) across all shell utilities.\n\nKey changes:\n- **Debug/Build.sh, Run.sh**: Remove tabs from `case` block bodies in Debug and Release profile definitions.\n- **Format.sh, Save.sh**: Standardize directory resolution to `>/dev/null` and fix `find` command piping in the shell formatter.\n- **Integration/SmokeProfiles.sh, Profile.sh, Release.sh**: Align `case` block indentation and merge split redirect operators for better readability.\n- **Script/CleanGenerated.sh, GenerateRouteManifest.sh**: Fix `grep`/`awk` piping and redirect spacing; standardize `find` output handling.\n- **Script/PostHogCapture.sh, ResolveIdentity.sh, SignBundle.sh**: Unify `2>/dev/null` usage and fix `codesign` command formatting in `SignBundle.sh`.\n\nThese changes ensure all shell scripts pass `shfmt` and `shellcheck` without warnings, improving CI reliability and code consistency.",
			"SHA": "dee3578f1d17eb95e8994be6b4e4bb0f4fb8094d"
		}
